<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" ?>
<Defs>
  <!--
    Templated from VFEP's VFEP_WarcasketHelmet_Controller (VFEP v4.03,
    1.6/Defs/ThingDefs_Misc/Apparel_Headgear.xml); fields not discussed here, uiIconScale and
    the toxic offset included, are the Controller's, its drone module left off. Plating, tags,
    the market-value references and the UltraMechtech gate follow the armor's header.

    Tuning: the piece is the set's answer to Biotech's mechlord helmet (MechBandwidth 12,
    ShootingAccuracyPawn -5, MeleeHitChance -0.5; Plasteel 120, ComponentSpacer 6,
    NanostructuringChip 2; UltraMechtech), which it replaces on a mechanitor's head, on the
    tier's plating and vacuum seal in place of the mechlord's recon-grade shell.
    - MechBandwidth 12, the mechlord helmet's. With the armor's 8 the set gives 20 against the
      mechlord pair's 24, the gap being what the resurrection core costs.
    - ShootingAccuracyPawn -3 / MeleeHitChance -1, vanilla's price for the bandwidth, leaned
      away from its -5 / -0.5. Both are skill levels added before the stat's curve, not
      percentages: the pilot shoots as if three Shooting levels lower and swings as if one Melee
      level lower. A warcasket pilot still fights, where the mechlord pair (-10 shooting) makes
      a commander who does not, so the shooting cost is lighter and the melee one heavier.
    - No PsychicSensitivity offset, where the Controller's helmet has -0.5. A mechlink needs a
      psychically sensitive brain: CompUseEffect_InstallImplant refuses the mechlink
      (requiresPsychicallySensitive) to a pawn at zero sensitivity, which the Controller's -0.5
      on helmet and armor together make of a baseline pilot. The lore has the link's psychic
      half engineered into the helmet; the armor keeps -0.2.
    - costList ComponentSpacer 6 / Plasteel 80 / NanostructuringChip 2: the mechlord helmet's
      components and chips (the apocriton's drop); the plasteel is the tier's helmet 60 plus 20
      for the mechanitor hardware, short of the mechlord's 120 because the shell is the
      chassis's own.

    Command range: the helmet declares no CommandRangeExtension. The shoulders carry it in XML
    (their header); it lands here at startup when the mod settings point the extended command
    range at the helmet.

    Art: the helmet alone of the three pieces ships masks (_northm/_eastm/_southm for the worn
    graphic, _m for the item icon), so it draws with CutoutComplex and useWornGraphicMask, as
    VFEP's Controller helmet does and as vanilla's prestige armors are the pattern: the
    CompColorable colour paints the mask's red areas and the black-masked trim keeps its painted
    colour (apparel graphics pass white as colorTwo). Mask names differ by graphic class:
    Graphic_Multi reads <path>_northm, Graphic_Single <path>_m.

    ApparelExtension priority 1, for the reason in the armor def's header: the
    VFEP_WarcasketHelmetBase parent carries its own, and only the highest-priority copy keeps
    its fields whole (Merge still ORs the parent's isUnifiedApparel and hideHead in). Any new
    ApparelExtension field for this piece goes on this entry.

    Compat: SOS2Patch.xml gives it the EVA tag and Insulation_Cold 100 alongside the armor;
    the VGE vacuum patch lowers its VacuumResistance to VGE1's warcasket-helmet value; the
    1.6/Mods/CombatExtended/Patches/ root rescales its plating and seals it against CE's
    smoke, which reads no tox immunity.
  -->
  <VFEPirates.WarcasketDef ParentName="VFEP_WarcasketHelmetBase">
    <defName>OLWC_WarcasketHelmet_Overlord</defName>
    <label>overlord warcasket helmet</label>
    <shortDescription>Specialized spacer-tech warcasket helmet with standard protection, equipped with signal enhancers that greatly increase the pilot's control bandwidth.</shortDescription>
    <description>Specialized spacer-tech warcasket helmet with standard protection, equipped with signal enhancers that greatly increase the pilot's control bandwidth.\n\nA 10th-generation design from the government program that rebuilt captured pirate rigs around its own power armor and gave them to veterans who could no longer serve any other way. The Overlord was its rig for veteran mechanitors, who would command their own mechs in the field rather than join a squad.\n\nThe Overlord series is meant for a mechanitor who goes into battle alone, with only their mechs beside them. The core in the shell holds only a few charges and regains them slowly, so they are best saved for the mechs that matter most. When a fight cannot wait, it can be reloaded with advanced components. The helmet greatly increases the pilot's bandwidth at some cost to their aim, the shoulders carry command relays that reach mechs anywhere on the map, and the arms are left free for smithing and hacking. Because the plating is far tougher than a mechanitor's usual armor, the pilot can lead from the front line rather than from behind the mechs.</description>
    <graphicData>
      <texPath>Things/Pawn/Warcasketlike/WarcasketOverlord/WarcasketOverlordHelmet</texPath>
      <shaderType>CutoutComplex</shaderType>
    </graphicData>
    <uiIconScale>1.25</uiIconScale>
    <statBases>
      <Mass>8</Mass>
      <ArmorRating_Sharp>2</ArmorRating_Sharp>
      <ArmorRating_Blunt>1</ArmorRating_Blunt>
      <ArmorRating_Heat>1</ArmorRating_Heat>
      <Insulation_Cold>10</Insulation_Cold>
      <Insulation_Heat>10</Insulation_Heat>
      <EquipDelay>1</EquipDelay>
    </statBases>
    <equippedStatOffsets>
      <MechBandwidth>12</MechBandwidth>
      <ShootingAccuracyPawn>-3</ShootingAccuracyPawn>
      <MeleeHitChance>-1</MeleeHitChance>
      <ToxicResistance>0.5</ToxicResistance>
      <SlaveSuppressionOffset MayRequire="Ludeon.RimWorld.Ideology">0.1</SlaveSuppressionOffset>
      <VacuumResistance MayRequire="Ludeon.RimWorld.Odyssey">0.7</VacuumResistance>
    </equippedStatOffsets>
    <costList>
      <ComponentSpacer>6</ComponentSpacer>
      <Plasteel>80</Plasteel>
      <NanostructuringChip>2</NanostructuringChip>
    </costList>
    <researchPrerequisites>
      <li>VFEP_SpacerWarcaskets</li>
      <li>UltraMechtech</li>
    </researchPrerequisites>
    <apparel>
      <bodyPartGroups>
        <li>FullHead</li>
      </bodyPartGroups>
      <wornGraphicPath>Things/Pawn/Warcasketlike/WarcasketOverlord/WarcasketOverlordHelmet</wornGraphicPath>
      <useWornGraphicMask>true</useWornGraphicMask>
      <layers>
        <li>Overhead</li>
      </layers>
      <tags>
        <li>WarcasketVeteran</li>
        <li>WarcasketAll</li>
      </tags>
    </apparel>
    <modExtensions>
      <li Class="VEF.Apparels.ApparelExtension">
        <priority>1</priority>
      </li>
    </modExtensions>
  </VFEPirates.WarcasketDef>
</Defs>
